// Test: Subtyping - Known (!) is subtype of Uncertain (?)
// Spec: 03-TYPES.md § 2.3 Subtyping
// Priority: P0
//
// Purpose:
// Validates that a Known (!) value can be assigned to an Uncertain (?)
// variable, demonstrating that T! <: T?
//
// Expected behavior:
// Should compile successfully and print 42

rite main() {
    ≔ x: !i32 = 42;
    ≔ y: ?i32 = x;  // Subtyping: !i32 <: ?i32
    println(y);
}
